literal   grid?   separates trunc/near at F=0 (W=3 unsigned sat)
    1/2    no     no   trunc=0 near=0
    3/4    no     SEPARATES   trunc=0 near=1
    1/3    no     no   trunc=0 near=0
    2/3    no     SEPARATES   trunc=0 near=1
    3/2    no     SEPARATES   trunc=1 near=2
    5/2    no     no   trunc=2 near=2
      1    yes    no   trunc=1 near=1
      2    yes    no   trunc=2 near=2

CONTROL: every grid literal must fail to separate -> PASS
CONTROL: at least one non-grid literal must separate -> PASS

The tie case: 1/2 is non-grid at F=0 and does NOT separate, because
ties-to-even sends it to 0 and truncation sends it to 0 as well.
So 'non-grid' is necessary and not sufficient; 'non-grid and not a tie' is the
condition, and any half-integer is exactly the excluded case.
